1	# term-project: team rules
2	
3	Team law for CS 370 (Colorado State University, Prof. Shrideep Pallickara), Fall 2026.
4	Both partners maintain this file. Claude Code reads it every session, so **a constraint that
5	lives only in one partner's head protects nothing.**
6	
7	This file is self-contained on purpose: a teammate who clones only this repo has everything
8	they need. (Nick has a separate personal course-notes folder one level up; that is not team law
9	and is not required to work in this repo.)
10	
11	---
12	
13	## Project status (update this as things get decided)
14	
15	- **Idea: LOCKED — Dark Sky Monitor.** An offline device that measures sky brightness and cloud
16	  cover at one site and grades the night GOOD / MARGINAL / POOR / UNKNOWN with the evidence behind
17	  the verdict. Full design review in [`docs/design-review.md`](docs/design-review.md).
18	- **Team:** Nick Marechal + Liam Sagal.
19	- **Where we left off: [`docs/progress-log.md`](docs/progress-log.md). Read it first.** Newest
20	  entry on top: milestone position, what code exists and what it guarantees, the shared record
21	  contract, and the open work. Add an entry there when you finish a chunk of work.
22	- **Hardware: two kits.** **`darksky.local`** (Nick: Pi 4 Model B **1 GB** + TSL2591 + MLX90614
23	  **3.3 V** + BME280; arrived 2026-10-13, set up headless 2026-10-27, I2C on, power `0x0`) is the
24	  **device of record**: the soak, the demo and every evaluation number come only from it.
25	  **`starlight.local`** (Liam's dev Pi + the same three sensors) is for parallel development only.
26	  **`darksky.local`: all three sensors wired and answering 2026-10-28** (`0x29`, `0x5a`, `0x76`;
27	  BME280 genuine). `starlight.local` not wired. DS3231 RTC to be ordered; until it is fitted the Pi
28	  takes real time from the network at boot. Enclosure still unbought. See
29	  [`docs/hardware-log.md`](docs/hardware-log.md) and [`docs/bill-of-materials.md`](docs/bill-of-materials.md).
30	- **Mechanisms: D** (crash-consistent storage) **+ E** (multiprocess + IPC + supervisor). C and F
31	  were considered and rejected — at 0.1–1 Hz sampling neither is justified, and being able to say
32	  why is a stronger defense answer than bolting them on.
33	- **Design: `DESIGN.md` M2 written 2026-10-27 (Liam).** The decisions in Nick's area (listed in
34	  the 2026-10-27 M2 entry of [`docs/progress-log.md`](docs/progress-log.md)) were confirmed by
35	  Nick on 2026-10-28. Values marked (a) are datasheet assumptions,
36	  not measurements. Record, IPC and supervision detail: [`docs/record-and-ipc.md`](docs/record-and-ipc.md).
37	- **Next action:** finish hardware-log §3–5 on `darksky.local` (§1–2 done 2026-10-28, which met
38	  M2's "both sensors electrically alive"). Step 4 (acrylic vs. LDPE film in front of the MLX90614) tests
39	  the largest hardware unknown in the project.
40	- **Open gap:** the problem memo names an archetype, not a named individual. Outreach to the
41	  Northern Colorado Astronomical Society / CSU astronomy faculty still pending.
42	
43	## Commands
44	
45	- Build: `make`            Deploy to Pi: `make deploy PI=pi@<host>`
46	- Tests: `make test`       Sanitizers: `make asan`      Valgrind: `make memcheck`
47	- Soak sanity: `make soakcheck` (1-hour miniature of the 48h run)
48	- **A change is DONE only when build, test, and asan pass. Show the output.**
49	
50	Targets exist and run today; several are no-ops until there is source to build. Do not let a
51	target silently become a lie — if it stops doing what its name says, fix it or rename it.
52	
53	## Hard constraints (graded — spec §3.3, §3.4)
54	
55	- The PRODUCT makes **no network calls except serving its own LAN interface**. No LLM APIs, no
56	  cloud inference, no pretrained models, no external weather/data APIs at runtime. The device
57	  must work with the network cable unplugged. The intelligence in `analysis/` is ours. A grader
58	  must be able to confirm this in one minute by reading the source tree.
59	  - Public data (NWS, USGS, etc.) may be used **only** as an offline ground-truth comparison
60	    while writing the evaluation report — never called from the device's own code.
61	- Every daemon must be **supervisable**: clean exit codes, no orphaned fds across restart,
62	  heartbeat within 60s of start.
63	- Every allocation checked; every syscall's error path handled and logged. The 48-hour soak is
64	  the test suite of last resort.
65	- **NEVER weaken, skip, or delete a test to make the suite pass.**
66	- Replayed or synthesized data is **labeled as such everywhere it appears** — in logs, in the
67	  report, in the demo. The 48h soak and the live demo run on live sensors.
68	
69	## Style
70	
71	- Systems core: **C17, `-Wall -Wextra -Werror`, no VLAs.** `goto`-cleanup for multi-resource
72	  functions. ASan/valgrind findings cap that component's score at 50%, so they are bugs, not
73	  warnings.
74	- Python permitted only under `tools/` and `ui/`. **No graded mechanism may live there.**
75	- Smallest diff that passes. Do not refactor unrelated code.
76	
77	## Ownership
78	
79	Ownership means **first authorship and answerability at the defense**, not exclusivity. Each
80	partner is individually examined on their own subsystems plus one question from across the
81	boundary.
82	
83	- **Nick:** `src/common/` (record format + CRC — owned by storage, used by everyone) and
84	  `src/store/` — mechanism **D**, the crash-consistent storage layer.
85	- **Liam (confirmed by Liam 2026-10-27):** `src/super/`, `src/sensors/`, and the IPC — mechanism
86	  **E**: the supervisor (`dskyd`), the sensor daemons, the shm rings, sockets and pipes, and
87	  `fusiond`'s ring-draining loop. All Linux-only I2C code lives in `src/sensors/`, so everything
88	  else builds and tests on a Mac.
89	- **Analysis and query CLI (proposed by Liam, confirmed by Nick 2026-10-28):** Liam: classifier +
90	  state machine. Nick: features, ephemeris, and the `dsq` query CLI.
91	- The agent edits outside the current session owner's area only when told explicitly whose
92	  session this is.
93	
94	## Workflow (spec §10, Assignment 0's nine steps apply verbatim)
95	
96	- Multi-file or algorithmic change: **plan first, wait for approval.** No code in the first pass.
97	- **Hardware bugs: paste real evidence** — `dmesg`, timing captures, `/proc/interrupts`, logic
98	  analyzer output. Never propose or accept a fix derived from a verbal description of a sensor
99	  problem. The agent will confidently reason about a sensor it has never met and be wrong in
100	  ways only an instrument catches.
101	- Commit only from a green state; message format `M<n>: <what>`.
102	- **≥ 40 meaningful commits** across the project, both partners well represented. A pair of
103	  "final submission" commits is an automatic process grade of **zero, for both partners.**
104	- Each partner works in **their own clone and their own Claude Code sessions.** Working in one
105	  shared login defeats the per-partner transcript grading and costs both of you.
106	- Every milestone's diffs get **two reviews**: a fresh-context agent review and a human review
107	  by the partner who did not write the code. Each partner's `PROMPTLOG.md` must record at least
108	  one review of the other's work.
109	
110	## Transcript discipline (do not skip — spec §6, §10.4)
111	
112	At **every** milestone M1–M5, each partner copies their raw `.jsonl` sessions from
113	`~/.claude/projects/<project-dir>/` into `transcripts/<partner>/`. As-is. Not summarized, not
114	exported, not retyped. See `transcripts/README.md`.
115	
116	Local transcripts purge after 30 days by default and this project spans more than 30 days.
117	Losing Week-5 transcripts in Week 15 is a foreseeable loss, and foreseeable losses are not
118	excused.
